    "content_units": [
      {
        "id": "u1",
        "kind": "ANALOGY",
        "label": "Gold Coins and Magic Whistle Analogy",
        "attributes": {},
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s1"
        ],
        "rationale": "Uses an analogy of gold coins mixed with mud being temporarily transformed into ghosts to explain the concept of selective volatilization and subsequent decomposition in vapour phase refining.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "social"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Hello! Welcome to our chemistry session. Today, we are going to look at a very clever technique used in metallurgy called **Vapour Phase Refining**. ",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 149
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "social"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Don't let the fancy name intimidate you. By the end of this, you’ll see it’s just a smart, two-step trick to get extremely pure metals!",
            "start": 151,
            "end": 286
          },
          {
            "id": "p3",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "separator"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "---",
            "start": 288,
            "end": 291
          },
          {
            "id": "p4",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### The Big Idea: An Analogy First",
            "start": 293,
            "end": 327
          },
          {
            "id": "p5",
            "category": "ANALOGY",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Imagine you have a bucket of gold coins mixed with wet mud and rocks. It’s hard to pick the mud off every single coin. ",
            "start": 328,
            "end": 447
          },
          {
            "id": "p6",
            "category": "ANALOGY",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Now, imagine you had a magic whistle that could turn *only* the gold coins into invisible ghosts that float up into the air, leaving the mud and rocks sitting at the bottom of the bucket. Then, in another room, you blow a second whistle that turns the ghosts back into solid, shiny, clean gold coins.",
            "start": 449,
            "end": 749
          },
          {
            "id": "p7",
            "category": "ANALOGY",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "That is **exactly** what Vapour Phase Refining does. ",
            "start": 751,
            "end": 804
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The analogy accurately captures the conceptual logic of converting a metal selectively to a gas phase while leaving impurities behind, followed by reconverting it to a pure solid.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u2",
        "kind": "CONCEPT",
        "label": "Definition and Purpose of Vapour Phase Refining",
        "attributes": {
          "depth": "explanation"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s2"
        ],
        "rationale": "Defines vapour phase refining as a method of converting impure metal into a volatile compound and decomposing it to recover pure metal, highlighting its purpose for ultra-high purity.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p8",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "separator"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "---",
            "start": 806,
            "end": 809
          },
          {
            "id": "p9",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### What is Vapour Phase Refining?",
            "start": 811,
            "end": 845
          },
          {
            "id": "p10",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "In simple terms: **It is a method where an impure metal is converted into a gas (vapour), separated from its impurities, and then broken down again to get the pure metal.**",
            "start": 846,
            "end": 1018
          },
          {
            "id": "p11",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "This is used when we need metals with **ultra-high purity** (for things like space technology or electronics).",
            "start": 1020,
            "end": 1130
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The definition and stated application for achieving ultra-high purity metals are chemically accurate.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u3",
        "kind": "CONCEPT",
        "label": "Requirements for Vapour Phase Refining",
        "attributes": {
          "depth": "explanation"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s2"
        ],
        "rationale": "Details the essential conditions required for vapour phase refining: formation of a volatile compound at lower temperature, ease of decomposition at higher temperature, and non-reactivity of impurities.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p12",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "separator"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "---",
            "start": 1132,
            "end": 1135
          },
          {
            "id": "p13",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### The Two Golden Rules",
            "start": 1137,
            "end": 1161
          },
          {
            "id": "p14",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "To use this method, the metal must follow two strict rules:",
            "start": 1162,
            "end": 1221
          },
          {
            "id": "p15",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1. **Easy to turn into gas:** The metal must easily react with a chemical at a relatively low temperature to form a **volatile compound** (a compound that turns into a gas easily).",
            "start": 1222,
            "end": 1402
          },
          {
            "id": "p16",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2. **Easy to break down:** That gas must easily decompose (break apart) at a higher temperature to give back the pure metal.",
            "start": 1403,
            "end": 1527
          },
          {
            "id": "p17",
            "category": "CAVEAT",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "qualification"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "*(Crucially: The impurities mixed with the metal must **not** react, so they stay behind as solids).*",
            "start": 1529,
            "end": 1630
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "Correctly states the two fundamental requirements and the qualification regarding unreactive impurities.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u4",
